IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- ca-interpretation-commencement.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: three rules about the start of an enactment that the first two passes left unasked.  Pass 3.
-- Section 5(4) (which provisions it deems to have come into force on the date of assent), section 7 (the permission to exercise a power
-- before commencement, of which the time module has only the "no effect until commencement" limb) and the Related Provisions item,
-- 1998, c. 30, s. 10 (a proceeding commenced before that section came into force).
-- Imports the standard library and `daydate` only: the time module's functions are not called here.
--
-- THE HOUSE RULE FOR A RULE THAT HAS A STATED CONDITION.  The answer is TRUE where the text states the condition and it is met.
-- It is FALSE only where the text says so in terms, with one deliberate exception marked where it occurs (section 5(4)'s own condition).
-- Where the case asked about is not one the text addresses, the answer is a refusal.
-- Each refusal is a named function at a generic type, so that its name says what the text leaves open.

§ `Section 5(4): the remaining provisions of an Act`

-- The subsection applies "where an Act provides that certain provisions thereof are to come or are deemed to have come into force on a day
-- other than the date of assent".  Then the remaining provisions, the ones not so provided for, are deemed to have come into force on the
-- date of assent.  If the Act gives no provision a day other than the date of assent, the subsection's condition is not met and it deems
-- nothing; the date of commencement is then the date of assent by subsection 5(2), which gives the same date.
-- The first function asks whether section 5(4) itself does the deeming for the provision asked about (the question is about the section's
-- own condition, so a condition not met is FALSE, not a refusal).  The second gives the date.
-- src:52 | (4) Where an Act provides that certain provisions thereof are to come or are deemed to have come into force on a day other than the date of assent to the Act, the remaining provisions of the Act are deemed to have come into force on the date of assent to the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act s 5(4) (src:52)
GIVEN `the Act provides that certain provisions of it are to come or are deemed to have come into force on a day other than the date of assent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision asked about is not one of those certain provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 5(4) deems a provision of an Act to have come into force on the date of assent, given that` `the Act provides that certain provisions of it are to come or are deemed to have come into force on a day other than the date of assent` `and` `the provision asked about is not one of those certain provisions` MEANS
        `the Act provides that certain provisions of it are to come or are deemed to have come into force on a day other than the date of assent`
    AND `the provision asked about is not one of those certain provisions`

-- src:52 | (4) Where an Act provides that certain provisions thereof are to come or are deemed to have come into force on a day other than the date of assent to the Act, the remaining provisions of the Act are deemed to have come into force on the date of assent to the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act s 5(4) (src:52)
GIVEN `the day the Act was assented to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date on which the remaining provisions of an Act are deemed to have come into force, the Act being assented to on` `the day the Act was assented to` MEANS
    `the day the Act was assented to`

§ `Section 7: a power exercised before commencement`

-- "Where an enactment is not in force and it contains provisions conferring power to make regulations or do any other thing, that power
-- may, for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement, be exercised at any time before its commencement."
-- The time module answers the second limb ("a regulation so made or a thing so done has no effect until the commencement ... except in
-- so far as may be necessary").  This function answers the first: the permission.
-- The permission covers a power "to make regulations" and a power "to do any other thing" alike, so the kind of power is an input that
-- does not change the answer.  It is conditioned three ways, all stated: the enactment is not yet in force, it contains the provisions
-- that confer the power, and the exercise is for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement.
-- Where one of the three fails, the text does not address the case (an exercise for another purpose is simply not within the permission,
-- and the Act does not say whether it is otherwise allowed), so the answer is a refusal and not FALSE.
DECLARE `A power an enactment not yet in force may confer` IS ONE OF
    `a power to make regulations`
    `a power to do any other thing`

-- src:66 | 7 Where an enactment is not in force and it contains provisions conferring power to make regulations or do any other thing, that power may, for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement, be exercised at any time before its commencement, but a regulation so made or a thing so done has no effect until the commencement of the enactment, except in so far as may be necessary to make the enactment effective on its commencement.
@ref Interpretation Act s 7 (src:66)
GIVEN k IS A `A power an enactment not yet in force may confer`
      `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power of the kind` k `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised` `and` `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power` `and` `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a power to make regulations` THEN
        `the three conditions of section 7 are met where` `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised` `and` `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power` `and` `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement`
    WHEN `a power to do any other thing` THEN
        `the three conditions of section 7 are met where` `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised` `and` `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power` `and` `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement`

-- src:66 | 7 Where an enactment is not in force and it contains provisions conferring power to make regulations or do any other thing, that power may, for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement, be exercised at any time before its commencement, but a regulation so made or a thing so done has no effect until the commencement of the enactment, except in so far as may be necessary to make the enactment effective on its commencement.
@ref Interpretation Act s 7 (src:66)
GIVEN `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the three conditions of section 7 are met where` `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised` `and` `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power` `and` `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement` MEANS
    IF       `the enactment is not in force when the power is exercised`
         AND `the enactment contains the provisions that confer the power`
         AND `the power is exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 7 permits an enactment not yet in force to have a power it confers exercised before commencement for the purpose of making it effective on commencement and says nothing of any other exercise`

-- src:66 | 7 Where an enactment is not in force and it contains provisions conferring power to make regulations or do any other thing, that power may, for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement, be exercised at any time before its commencement, but a regulation so made or a thing so done has no effect until the commencement of the enactment, except in so far as may be necessary to make the enactment effective on its commencement.
@ref Interpretation Act s 7 (src:66): any other exercise is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 7 permits an enactment not yet in force to have a power it confers exercised before commencement for the purpose of making it effective on commencement and says nothing of any other exercise` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 7 permits an enactment not yet in force to have a power it confers exercised before commencement for the purpose of making it effective on commencement and says nothing of any other exercise"

§ `Related Provisions, 1998, c. 30, s. 10: a proceeding commenced before that section came into force`

-- Plain gloss: a proceeding that was commenced before the section came into force, and in respect of which a provision amended by sections 12
-- to 16 of that Act applies, is taken up and continued under, and in conformity with, that amended provision, without any further formality.
-- The item is operative text: it tells the court or authority before which such a proceeding is pending how to carry it on.  Pass 1 and the
-- first part of pass 2 filed it as `inert` because "it affects no one now"; that is not a reason the brief allows, and a proceeding of that
-- age could in principle still be running.  It is encoded here (corrected 2026-10-29).
-- The text gives no commencement date for the section, so the day it came into force is an input.  Section 6(1) of this Act, which applies to
-- the 1998 Act as to any enactment (s 3(1)), makes an enactment expressed to come into force on a day come into force on the expiration
-- of the day before, so the section is in force from the first moment of that day: a proceeding commenced on an earlier day was commenced
-- before the coming into force, and one commenced on that day or later was not.
-- The text says what happens to the proceeding commenced before.  It says nothing of a proceeding commenced on or after the day the section
-- came into force, or of one in respect of which no amended provision applies, so those refuse.
-- "Without any further formality" is stated in terms: a further formality is not needed, so that is FALSE, but only for the case the section addresses.
-- src:501 | — 1998, c. 30, s. 10
-- src:502 | Transitional — proceedings
-- src:503 | 10 Every proceeding commenced before the coming into force of this section and in respect of which any provision amended by sections 12 to 16 applies shall be taken up and continued under and in conformity with that amended provision without any further formality.
@ref Interpretation Act, Related Provisions, 1998, c. 30, s. 10 (src:501-503)
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the first day on which the section is in force` IS A DATE
      `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `where the section is first in force on` `the first day on which the section is in force` `and` `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to the proceeding` MEANS
    IF       `the day the proceeding was commenced` LESS THAN `the first day on which the section is in force`
         AND `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to the proceeding`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `the section speaks of a proceeding commenced before it came into force in respect of which a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 applies and says nothing of any other`

